-- title:
--   A common domain for the branch function field and k(jmath̃)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$ and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a package of data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field of level $p$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O$ for the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$, write $C$ for the curve of the package's curve model $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k$ over $k$, and let $\xi \in X_O$ be the image of the generic point of $C$ under the morphism $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap` $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ (the base-change morphism from the pullback over $k$ to the pullback over $O$ induced by $\mathrm{to}\kappa$). Let $\psi$ be a ring homomorphism from the residue field $\kappa(\xi)$ of the stalk of $X_O$ at $\xi$ to `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k$ and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,1$. Assume that $\psi$ reads the $O$-constants through $\mathrm{to}\kappa$: for every $a \in O$, the value of $\psi$ on the residue class of the germ at $\xi$ of the image of $a$ under the global sections of the second projection of $X_O$ equals the image of $\mathrm{to}\kappa(a)$ in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`; and assume that $\psi$ takes at least one value outside the image of $k$. Then there are a commutative domain $D$, ring homomorphisms $\iota_k : k \to D$ and $\iota_\kappa : \kappa(\xi) \to D$, and ring homomorphisms $\Theta : D \to C.\mathrm{functionField}$ and $\Psi : D \to$ `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` such that: $\Theta \circ \iota_k$ is the canonical embedding of $k$ into the function field of $C$ obtained from the structure morphism of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k$ (the germ at the generic point of the image of a constant); $\Theta \circ \iota_\kappa$ is the map on residue fields induced by the stalk map of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap` $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ at the generic point of $C$; $\Psi \circ \iota_k$ is the structural embedding of $k$ into `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`; $\Psi \circ \iota_\kappa = \psi$; $\Theta$ is injective; every element of $C.\mathrm{functionField}$ is of the form $\Theta(a)/\Theta(b)$ with $\Theta(b) \ne 0$; and $\Psi$ is injective.
--
--   This is the descent step expressing that the residue field at the generic point of the chosen component of the Deligne–Rapoport fibre generates, over $k$, both the function field of the component's model $C$ and, through $\psi$, the level-one fibre field inside $k((q))$: the intended domain is the tensor product of $k$ with $\kappa(\xi)$ over the residue field of $O$, and the injectivity of $\Psi$ follows from that of $\Theta$ since the function field of $C$ has transcendence degree one over $k$ and $\psi$ is non-constant. It is used in the construction of the ring isomorphisms with a rational function field that identify the stalk maps at the generic points of the two labelled components of the fibre.
